## 8. VIVA QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS

Q1. What is Pandas?
Ans. Pandas is a Python library used for data manipulation and analysis. It provides Series and DataFrame structures.

Q2. What is a DataFrame?
Ans. A DataFrame is a two-dimensional tabular data structure containing rows and columns.

Q3. Which function is used to read a CSV file?
Ans. pd.read_csv().

Q4. Which function is used to read an Excel file?
Ans. pd.read_excel().

Q5. Which function is used to read a JSON file?
Ans. pd.read_json().

Q6. What is JSON?
Ans. JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation. It is a text-based format used to store and exchange structured data.

Q7. What is the use of concat()?
Ans. concat() combines two or more Pandas objects along a selected axis. Here, it combines datasets row-wise.

Q8. What does ignore_index=True do?
Ans. It creates a new continuous index after combining the DataFrames.

Q9. What is a missing value?
Ans. A missing value represents data that is unavailable or not recorded.

Q10. What is the use of fillna()?
Ans. fillna() replaces missing values with a specified value or calculated statistic.

Q11. Why is the median used for Quantity?
Ans. The median is less affected by extreme values than the mean and can be useful for filling missing numerical values.

Q12. What does drop_duplicates() do?
Ans. It removes duplicate rows from a DataFrame.

Q13. What is the purpose of pd.to_datetime()?
Ans. It converts date values into Pandas datetime format.

Q14. What is groupby()?
Ans. groupby() divides data into groups based on one or more columns and allows aggregate calculations.

Q15. What is a box plot?
Ans. A box plot summarizes a numerical distribution using the median, quartiles, and possible outliers.

